{"vasarupostriyam": [{"id": "vA'sarUpo'striyAm", "headword": "वाऽसरूपोऽस्त्रियाम्", "headword_slp1": "vA'sarUpo'striyAm", "fold": "vasarupostriyam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In this portion of the sūtras, in which there is reference to verbal roots, an affix which is calculated to debar a general one, not being of the same form, optionally debars it; but not so in the case of feminine affixes -- स्त्रियां क्तिन् ३.३.९४.\n\nTerms:", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वाऽसरूपोऽस्त्रियाम् ३.१.९४", "३.१.९४", "३.१.९४ वाऽसरूपोऽस्त्रियाम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA'sarUpo'striyAm ३.१.९४", "३.१.९४", "३.१.९४ vA'sarUpo'striyAm"]}], "vasantadiByasWak": [{"id": "vasantAdiByazWak", "headword": "वसन्तादिभ्यष्ठक्", "headword_slp1": "vasantAdiByazWak", "fold": "vasantadiByasWak", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who studies or who knows' after the words वसन्त etc.\n\nTerms: ठक्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वसन्तादिभ्यष्ठक् ४.२.६३", "४.२.६३", "४.२.६३ वसन्तादिभ्यष्ठक्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vasantAdiByazWak ४.२.६३", "४.२.६३", "४.२.६३ vasantAdiByazWak"]}], "vasantaca": [{"id": "vasantAcca", "headword": "वसन्ताच्च", "headword_slp1": "vasantAcca", "fold": "vasantaca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after the word वसन्त।\n\nTerms: छन्दस्-ठञ्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वसन्ताच्च ४.३.२०", "४.३.२०", "४.३.२० वसन्ताच्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vasantAcca ४.३.२०", "४.३.२०", "४.३.२० vasantAcca"]}], "vasudevarjunaByan vun": [{"id": "vAsudevArjunAByAM vun", "headword": "वासुदेवार्जुनाभ्यां वुन्", "headword_slp1": "vAsudevArjunAByAM vun", "fold": "vasudevarjunaByan vun", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'this is his object of veneration' after the words 1. वासुदेव and अर्जुना।\n\nTerms: वुञ्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वासुदेवार्जुनाभ्यां वुन् ४.३.९८", "४.३.९८", "४.३.९८ वासुदेवार्जुनाभ्यां वुन्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vAsudevArjunAByAM vun ४.३.९८", "४.३.९८", "४.३.९८ vAsudevArjunAByAM vun"]}], "vasnakrayavikrayawWan": [{"id": "vasnakrayavikrayAwWan", "headword": "वस्नक्रयविक्रयाट्ठन्", "headword_slp1": "vasnakrayavikrayAwWan", "fold": "vasnakrayavikrayawWan", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ठन् comes in the sense of 'he lives thereby' after the words 1. वस्न 2. क्रय and 3. विक्रय being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.\n\nTerms: ठन्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वस्नक्रयविक्रयाट्ठन् ४.४.१३", "४.४.१३", "४.४.१३ वस्नक्रयविक्रयाट्ठन्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vasnakrayavikrayAwWan ४.४.१३", "४.४.१३", "४.४.१३ vasnakrayavikrayAwWan"]}], "vasan gataH": [{"id": "vaSaM gataH", "headword": "वशं गतः", "headword_slp1": "vaSaM gataH", "fold": "vasan gataH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'gone' after the word वश 'control', being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.\n\nTerms: यत्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वशं गतः ४.४.८६", "४.४.८६", "४.४.८६ वशं गतः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vaSaM gataH ४.४.८६", "४.४.८६", "४.४.८६ vaSaM gataH"]}], "vasoH samuhe ca": [{"id": "vasoH samUhe ca", "headword": "वसोः समूहे च", "headword_slp1": "vasoH samUhe ca", "fold": "vasoH samuhe ca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'a collection' after the word वसु , as well as with the force of मतुप् , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).\n\nTerms: यत्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वसोः समूहे च ४.४.१४०", "४.४.१४०", "४.४.१४० वसोः समूहे च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vasoH samUhe ca ४.४.१४०", "४.४.१४०", "४.४.१४० vasoH samUhe ca"]}], "vasnadravyaByan WankanO": [{"id": "vasnad